Title:
N0xis — AI-first reverse-engineering toolkit (static analysis, SSA decompiler, live memory provenance)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
N0xis is a CLI-first reverse-engineering toolkit that links live-process memory observations (scans/watchpoints/breakpoints) to static analysis results (function discovery, SSA decompilation) in a single scriptable workflow. Its core value is “provenance”: starting from an address that changes in memory, it traces the write back to the exact instruction, resolves the containing function, and returns decompiled context as JSON suitable for automation. It supports PE and ELF on Windows and Linux, and can operate on static files, live PIDs, snapshots, or remote targets over SSH using the same analysis pipeline. The project emphasizes verifiability with an “oracle” corpus and measured comparisons against external ground truth (objdump/LLVM disassemblers, unwind tables, exports, RTTI strings). It also includes name recovery (RTTI, NativeAOT mappings, select runtime formats) and persistence/diffing via versioned tables and caching. Useful for reverse engineers, red teamers, and malware analysts who need fast root-cause mapping from runtime behavior to code.

Technical Focus:
- Live memory scanning (value/pointer/AOB), snapshot narrowing, patching/freezing
- Hardware/software/conditional breakpoints and watchpoints; cross-process stack unwinding
- SSA-based decompilation (Memory-SSA, phi-web coalescing, SSA destruction, branch recovery) with explainable optimizations
- Function discovery and extents via unwind metadata (.pdata/.eh_frame), exports, and PDB-assisted naming
- Symbol/name recovery: C++ RTTI (MSVC + Itanium), .NET NativeAOT method mapping, runtime-specific formats (e.g., IL2CPP, LuaJIT)
- JSON-first automation + MCP server (JSON-RPC over stdio) for agent/tool integration

Use Cases:
- Trace a decrypted/decoded buffer in RAM back to the decryption routine and decompile it
- Identify which code path writes to a sensitive variable/flag using hardware watchpoints
- Rapid triage of stripped binaries by recovering function boundaries and partial names
- Automate RE pipelines (discover → decompile → provenance trace) with JSON + jq scripting
- Diff functions/versions across builds using persisted analysis tables and caching
- Remote analysis of targets over SSH with consistent static/live workflows

Keywords:
reverse engineering, binary analysis, SSA decompiler, Memory SSA, provenance tracing, hardware watchpoint, breakpoint, AOB scan, process memory, PE, ELF, PDB, CodeView, unwind tables, .pdata, .eh_frame, RTTI, Itanium ABI, MSVC ABI, NativeAOT, IL2CPP, LuaJIT, JSON-RPC, MCP server, Rust